            "review_title": "Review at Buffet Cuu Van Long Premium",
            "review_text": "Monica\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam6 contributions\n0\nFood is awesome, but the accountant ruined it\nNov 2025 • Business\nThe restaurant is often crowded; you'll need to make a reservation to ensure a dining experience. The restaurant is renowned for its delicious fresh seafood in the Vietnamese foodies community. Restaurant staff are supportive and friendly. Highly recommend you try their flower crab, it's the most delicious and freshest dish. The normal crab is a bit off; I even smell the coffee taste in its meat.\n\nHowever, if you are a corporation that needs a legit VAT invoice, then you should deeply reconsider, since the accounting service is terrible.\n\nThere is a point that makes me pissed off, which is the accountant's attitude. I dined in the restaurant on 22/11, and asked for the corporate VAT invoice. In the past, my company got the VAT a day after. But unfortunately, this time, 27/11, there's nothing in my email. After contacting the fan page, they reassured me that the VAT will be sent to my mailbox. I have been waiting for their email for 5 days. The thing that really pisses me off is the accountant's attitude. She seems to be clueless. The restaurant must review the communication progress between the customer service with the accounting department. Particularly, the accountant's attitude. 想顾客尊重自己先要看自己工作能力和态度。职业差，倚老卖老的会计师。\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nBooking first. Must take the retail invoice pic to ask for the VAT invoice! The accountant service is terrible.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten November 27, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
